------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prompt's templated native path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/` has no
matching Xcode target in this repo. The Apple app is a single SwiftUI source root
`apps/apple/Sources/` (project.yml `sources: - path: Sources`) shared by the iOS and
macOS app targets, with tests under `apps/apple/Tests/Unit`. To make the surface
actually compile + test under the gate's `xcodebuild ... build test`, the files were
placed in the real compiled roots and decomposed one-concern-per-file (swiftlint
`file_length` <= 400):

  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/Widgets/BatteryGaugeProjection.swift   (pure model)
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/Widgets/BatteryRadialGaugeModel.swift  (S8 binding)
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/Widgets/BatteryRadialGaugeContent.swift(SwiftUI views)
  apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/Widgets/BatteryRadialGaugeWidget.swift (entry + metadata)
  apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Dashboard/BatteryRadialGaugeWidgetTests.swift          (24 unit tests)

Data binds to the shared P1/S8 `VehiclesStore` via `StateHolderModel`/`LoadableState`
(no HTTP in the view). i18n resolves through the P1/S10 catalog `translation.widget.*`
+ `translation.common.{retry,refresh,offline}`, `translation.error.loadFailed`,
`translation.live.staleBanner.title` (all verified present in Localizable.xcstrings).
`view.opened` telemetry uses surface slug `BatteryRadialGaugeWidget` (P1/S11 seam).
Note: `charge_limit_soc` is absent from the frozen OpenAPI `VehicleState` contract, so the
charge-limit ring is inert on native (projection supports it for parity + tests).

States reproduced from the web source: loading (skeleton), empty ("No battery data"),
error (retry affordance), stale (chip + retained value), offline (cached value + chip),
plus charging indicator and the expanded-tile stat row.

