MAC_EXIT=70

  >> PRE-EXISTING, NON-SURFACE ENVIRONMENT BLOCK (documented, not a defect in this widget):
     (1) The macOS app + widget extension carry entitlements (app sandbox / keychain / push)
         that require a real Apple developer certificate + provisioning profile. project.yml
         pins DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="" and no signing identity exists on this runner, so the macOS
         app cannot be signed/provisioned here. This blocks ANY macOS `build test` in this repo
         on this runner, independent of this surface.
     (2) Separately, the XcodeGen-generated macOS unit-test TEST_HOST points at
         `TeslaSync-macOS.app/Contents/MacOS/TeslaSync-macOS`, but the macOS app PRODUCT_NAME is
         `TeslaSync`, so the real product is `TeslaSync.app/Contents/MacOS/TeslaSync` (the iOS
         test target already uses the correct `TeslaSync.app` path — which is why iOS passes).

